Let the PIN page pair without a uniqueid and report status accurately.

GET /pin still baked the placeholder id 0123456789ABCDEF into the page when
?uniqueid= was omitted, bypassing /submit-pin's waiting-client lookup for
desktop clients (moonlight-qt) and breaking pairing if /pin was opened before
clicking Pair. Leaves uniqueid blank when omitted, hides the Client ID line,
treats empty uniqueid= as omitted in /submit-pin, updates the non-blocking
success text to match the control panel, surfaces 400/404/409 error text, and
fixes submit-button error/edit handling.

Not upstream yet. Stacked on pairing-attempts-end.patch.

